
## 📊 Dataset Information

This project uses the **SDFVD (Small-scale Deepfake Forgery Video Dataset)** for training and evaluation.

- **Dataset Name:** Small-scale Deepfake Forgery Video Dataset (SDFVD)  
- **Source:** Mendeley Data  
- **Link:** https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/bcmkfgct2s/1  

### 📂 Dataset Description
The dataset contains a collection of real and deepfake videos created using face manipulation techniques. It is designed for research and educational purposes in deepfake detection.

### 🧾 Key Features
- Contains both **real** and **fake** videos  
- Includes **facial manipulations** such as face swapping and expression changes  
- Suitable for **frame-level analysis and temporal modeling**  
- Small-scale dataset, ideal for academic projects and experimentation  

### ⚙️ Usage in This Project
- Videos are converted into frames using OpenCV  
- Faces are extracted from each frame  
- Extracted face data is used to generate features  
- Features are labeled as **Real (0)** or **Fake (1)** for model training  

### ⚠️ Note
Due to dataset size and computational constraints, only a subset of videos may be used during training in Google Colab.

